  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>u</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>w</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> be vectors in three-dimensional space, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>u</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> are unit vectors which are not perpendicular to each other and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>u</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#183;</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>w</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#183;</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>w</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>w</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#183;</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>w</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>.<br />If the volume of the parallelopiped, whose adjacent sides are represented by the vectors <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>u</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>w</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>, is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>|</mo><mn>3</mn><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>u</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>|</mo></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
